filex-office-editor (scripts/x2t), BRF Tech, 2026-10-10: a frame's anchor
(text:anchor-type) is read from the frame whether or not it has a graphic
style.

Measured (2026-10-10): an odt whose formula frame has no draw:style-name -
<text:p>Toplam: <draw:frame text:anchor-type="as-char">...formula...
</draw:frame></text:p> - came into the document as a floating text box at
the top left of the page's margin (wp:anchor, posOffset 0, wrapSquare), so
the editor drew the formula in front of the sentence it ends.
common_draw_docx_convert (OdfFile/Reader/Format/draw_frame_docx.cpp) read the
frame's anchor only inside "if (graphicProperties)", which is empty for a
frame without a style; the frame was then not inline. LibreOffice gives
every frame a style (fr1, parent "Formula"), so its files kept their place;
other producers need not. With the anchor read first, an "as-char" formula
is inline (the OOXML math in the paragraph where the frame is), and a frame
anchored to the paragraph, the page or a character is placed relative to it
as one with a style is.

git apply reads from the first "diff --git" line on.

diff --git a/OdfFile/Reader/Format/draw_frame_docx.cpp b/OdfFile/Reader/Format/draw_frame_docx.cpp
index 8b3f66d..cc6464d 100644
--- a/OdfFile/Reader/Format/draw_frame_docx.cpp
+++ b/OdfFile/Reader/Format/draw_frame_docx.cpp
@@ -836,7 +836,13 @@ void common_draw_docx_convert(oox::docx_conversion_context & Context, union_comm
 		pagePropertiesNode ? pagePropertiesNode->attlist_ : emptyPageProperties;
 
 /////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
-	_CP_OPT(anchor_type) anchor;
+	// filex-office-editor (BRF Tech, 2026-10-10): the frame's own anchor
+	// (text:anchor-type is an attribute of the frame), whether or not the
+	// frame has a graphic style. It was read only inside the block below, so a
+	// frame without draw:style-name - a formula "as-char" at the end of a
+	// sentence - lost its anchor and became a floating shape at the top left
+	// of the page's margin, in front of the sentence.
+	_CP_OPT(anchor_type) anchor = attlists_.shape_with_text_and_styles_.common_text_anchor_attlist_.type_;
 	_CP_OPT(run_through) styleRunThrough;
 
 	if (graphicProperties)
@@ -851,7 +857,6 @@ void common_draw_docx_convert(oox::docx_conversion_context & Context, union_comm
 		}
 
 		styleRunThrough = graphicProperties->style_run_through_;
-		anchor = attlists_.shape_with_text_and_styles_.common_text_anchor_attlist_.type_;
 
 		drawing->styleHorizontalRel = graphicProperties->common_horizontal_rel_attlist_.style_horizontal_rel_;
 		drawing->styleHorizontalPos = graphicProperties->common_horizontal_pos_attlist_.style_horizontal_pos_;
